# CARDIODIAG Research Extension

This repository preserves the original CARDIODIAG notebooks and datasets while
adding a separate, leakage-controlled research implementation. The research
implementation is not a clinical diagnostic device and must not be used for
patient care.

## Current status

The initial audit is documented in `docs/initial_audit.md`. The current
research extension combines training-only stability analysis of the paper's
XAIH-DRC feature reduction with an empirical selective-reliability layer. The
current contribution is framed as a stability--reliability decoupling audit:
feature-set stability is tested separately from predictive reliability. The
result is mixed across the two development benchmarks, the uncertainty result
is internal only, and no external clinical validation is claimed yet. See
`docs/contribution_and_evidence.md` for the falsifiable hypotheses and generated
evidence.

## Setup

```text
uv venv --python 3.11 .venv
uv sync
```

## Checks

```text
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check src tests
```

See `docs/roadmap.md` for the experimental gates and `docs/dataset_provenance.md`
for provenance and external-validation rules.

When an independent dataset is frozen, evaluate it only through the gated
one-way runner in `experiments/run_external_evaluation.py`; it fits and
calibrates on development data and never fits on external rows.

## One-command internal stage

After setup, run the development-only nested validation stage with:

```text
uv run python experiments/run_internal_stage.py
```

This evaluates only the two existing benchmark datasets, writes JSON results
and a stage manifest under `results/generated/`, and does not perform or claim
external validation. Review `docs/execution_plan.md` before freezing any
external dataset or research conclusion.
